  "description": "The Pendulum 20th's attack table, measured: fifteen battles against a real Pendulum Ver.20th, one per point of the tap meter, with what the Digimon fired read off the screen each round (utilities/DIGIROM/pen20pattern.txt). Charges 0-6 were mapped twice, on two different Digimon after the first died, and matched -- the table belongs to the charge, not to the pet.\n\n**It is not DM20's.** Not one of the fifteen rows matches, which is what CLAUDE.md had assumed. A filmed battle settles it independently: the device's bar ran 10 -> 7 -> 4 -> 0, which is this table's row 10 exactly and not DM20's.\n\nA value is the attack and the attack is its damage: 1 single weak, 2 single strong, 3 double weak, 4 double strong. Critical is a fifth attack that only Tag Battles reach, so it never appears here.\n\nMeters 0, 5, 9 and 14 are pure rows of one attack each, which is a shape DM20's table does not have.",
